# Third NPC source, also superseded as of the chapter 59 release. docs/v2/
# keeps its grounding docs (world_state / party / planning / campaign_state /
# threads) in the palace — only its npcs/ subdir is excluded, so entities
# come from exactly one place. v2/npcs/ was last updated 2026-06-29 and had
# 124+ entities duplicated in merged_dossiers; leaving both mined meant a
# ~4-week-stale dossier could outrank the current one on a query.
# COVERAGE: verified good (2026-07-27). An earlier version of this comment
# claimed `brother_vareth`, `asha_vandry` and `blind_monk` were lost by this
# exclusion. RETRACTED — all three are reachable:
#   brother_vareth -> npc_vareth.md          (honorific dropped in the merge)
#   asha_vandry    -> npc_asha_vandree.md    (spelling normalised)
#   blind_monk     -> no dossier, but the scene is in the narrative wing
#                     (chapter_55_...) which CLAUDE.md treats as authoritative
# The bad claim came from grepping the FULL v2 filename against
# merged_dossiers. Grep the distinctive component (`vareth`, not
# `brother_vareth`) — the merge drops honorifics and normalises spelling.
# Also note v2/npcs/ stores variants of one entity as separate files
# (vareth.md AND brother_vareth.md; asha.md, asha_vandree.md AND
# asha_vandry.md), so a raw name-set diff overstates any gap. Query the
# palace before declaring something missing. See MEMPALACE_HORIZON.md.
docs/v2/npcs/

